From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:54:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] droid-extevdev: a microphone switch alone is a headset

MediaTek's accdet driver (mt6358-accdet.c and its siblings in the
vendor kernels) reports a 4-pole headset as SND_JACK_MICROPHONE only:
the input device sees SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT=1 and never
SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT. notify_ports() required the headphone (or
line-out) switch as well before calling it a headset, so on those
devices output-wired_headset, input-wired_headset and the headphone
ports all stayed unavailable with a headset plugged in, and nothing
above PulseAudio could tell anything was in the jack.

Android's WiredAccessoryManager maps SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT on its own
to BIT_HEADSET, the same as headphone and microphone together, which
is what these kernels are written against. Do the same: the headset
ports follow the microphone switch, and the headphone ports keep
meaning a plug without a microphone, so the two stay exclusive.

Seen on the Zinwa Q25 (mt6789/mt6366): dmesg logs "accdet
MICROPHONE(4-pole) PlugIn" and the jack's evdev node reports
SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT 1 and 0, while both wired ports stayed
"not available" until this change.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/droid/droid-extevdev.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/droid/droid-extevdev.c b/src/droid/droid-extevdev.c
index d192d0c..b05ebf5 100644
--- a/src/droid/droid-extevdev.c
+++ b/src/droid/droid-extevdev.c
@@ -135,9 +135,13 @@ static void notify_ports(pa_droid_extevdev *u) {
             pa_device_port_set_available(p, has_headphone);
     }
 
+    /* A microphone switch on its own is a headset too: MediaTek's accdet
+     * reports a 4-pole plug as SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT alone, without
+     * SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT, and Android's WiredAccessoryManager maps that to
+     * BIT_HEADSET just like both bits together. Requiring the headphone bit
+     * as well meant a headset was never seen on those devices. */
     pa_available_t has_headset =
-        ((u->sw_headphone_insert || u->sw_lineout_insert)
-        && u->sw_microphone_insert) ? PA_AVAILABLE_YES : PA_AVAILABLE_NO;
+        u->sw_microphone_insert ? PA_AVAILABLE_YES : PA_AVAILABLE_NO;
 
     for (i=0; i < N_ELEMENTS(headset_ports); i++) {
         pa_device_port *p = pa_hashmap_get(u->card->ports, headset_ports[i]);
-- 
